== F6-F8, D1, D4: jet debug's console

$ jet debug --break fib.jet:6 fib.jet -- 20  <<< 'p n\np n + 1\nwatch n\nbt\nq\n'
Breakpoint set  fib.jet:6
Breakpoint hit  fib.jet:6  in fib()
6 |     if n < 2 -> return n        <- here
Locals:  n = 30
(Jet) p n
n = 30
(Jet) p n + 1
`n + 1` is not a local here
(Jet) watch n
Unknown command `watch`. Commands: step (s), next (n), continue (c), finish (f), break N (b N), locals, print NAME (p NAME), backtrace (bt), help (h), quit (q)
(Jet) bt
#0  fib()  at fib.jet:6
#1  run()  at fib.jet:13
(Jet) q
Error [jet.DebugSessionQuit]: The `jet debug` session ended before the program finished — you typed `quit` at the `(Jet)` prompt.
 Why: Quitting the debugger stops the debugged program; it did not run to completion.
 Fix: Run `jet debug <file>` again and use `continue` (or `c`) to run to the end, or `jet run <file>` to run it without the debugger.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2204
(exit 1)

